================================================================================
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.generic_greeting=Hello, §o%s!
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.farmer.0=I am used to tough, back-breaking labor, that puts food on the table. Sowing seeds, tending to crops and coaxing life from the soil, is my life's calling.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.farmer.1=It became too cramped for me at home, so I gladly accept your invitation. I can help the people nurture the land to provide sustenance for us all.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.farmer.2=My family sent me here to make myself useful. I find joy in the cycles of life and am adept at working with plants but I don't shy away from hard work either.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.butcher.0=At home I was the bridge between the beast and the feast. I take pride in my craft, ensuring that every cut I offer is of the highest quality and I am happy to be here. 
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.butcher.1=My skilled hands are no longer needed at my hometown. I am a culinary artist who wields the knife with finesse and precision, here to offer my services
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.butcher.2=If there's something to do, I'm on hand. If it has to do with meat, even better. I take pride in sourcing the finest meats, ensuring they are expertly prepared

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.florist.0=I look forward to meeting you in person. With delicate hands and a keen eye, I am ready to help you build up this place, or even better, beautify it.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.florist.1=My passion lies in arranging petals and stems into breathtaking compositions. So if your new town have space for a passionate soul, count me in.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.florist.2=For generations, my ancestors have been storytellers in the language of flowers. So with my help in your village, we never get bored.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.fisherman.0=I would be happy to join your settlement. For a long time I was a humble servant of the sea and bring with me a lot of experience of hard work.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.fisherman.1=For a few years I served my people as seeker of the ocean's secrets. Providing for the hungry souls on land. Now the call of the sirens has brought me here.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.fisherman.2=I have tamed the tempestuous waters. Within these shores, I offer a glimpse into the world of the sea's harvest. May my skills be of use for your people.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.hunter.0=Whether you are in need of fresh game for a feast or guidance on the ways of the wilderness, you can count on me. My steady hand and sharp senses never disappointed me.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.hunter.1=I recieved a letter from you and would like to help building a new village. I can provide provisions for your travels or good advice on surviving the perils of the wilderness.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.hunter.2=The lands I am from became too small for me. I am a steward of the wild, a protector of the delicate balance between predator and prey and here to find a new home.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.vintner.0=A drought drove me from my home. Now I am here to help us both prosper. I used to work as a weaver of flavors and aromas, bottled to dazzle the senses.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.vintner.1=I had little success in the big town. Maybe this place is right suited for a provider of the nectar of the gods. A nectar as captivating as it is intoxicating.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.vintner.2=I am glad you invited me. Much more than my labor, I can impart knowledge about the alchemy of turning grapes into liquid poetry. Provided your soil allows it 

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.miller.0=My services are needed in many places. Transforming nature's bounty into the sustenance that feeds the village is a back-breaking labor, but I am ready to help.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.miller.1=Invaders destroyed our village. So my brothers and I moved apart, each in search of work and a home. I used to shape wheat into flour but any work is fine with me.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.miller.2=On this fertile land there is only one thing missing: a steward of the grain and the fields. Let me help this land grow and feed its hard working people

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.blacksmith.0=I spend my days shaping metal with fire and hammer, creating the finest tool. But any craft is fine with me, if you have a place for me to stay.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.blacksmith.1=I lost my home to invaders and now seeking refuge. I've been working the forge for as long as I can remember and sure be of good use for this place.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.blacksmith.2=For generations, my family has wielded the hammer and anvil, turning raw ore into objects of power. Now its time for me to find a place to lend a hand.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.lumberjack.0=I am glad you wrote. Back at home my duty was providing timber for construction, warmth for the hearth, and a livelihood for the community. Let me be of use here.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.lumberjack.1=If you're in need of logs for your hearth or tales of the forest to ignite your imagination, then you do well letting me live with you.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.lumberjack.2=My last contracts expired, so I'm here to find new ways to earn a living. In the past, the sturdiest trunks couldn't withstand my axe blows but any work will do.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.mason.0=If there's something to build, you called the right person. At home they call me the sculptor of stone and a builder of dreams. Where do we start?
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.mason.1=My family sent me here. For generations, my kind has wielded chisels an mallets and now my time has come to make myself useful.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.mason.2=I heard that you could use someone with skilled hands. I bring strength and beauty to structures that stand the test of time. Let me bring your visions to life

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.miner.0=I heard you gather workers for a new project. Lend me a pickaxe and I dig through the badrock itself. For enough food and a warm bed, of course. 
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.miner.1=Rumor has it you're interested in digging deep into the earth and unearthing its treasures. Well let me lend a hand.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.miner.2=Let me settle down with you. I am well acquainted with rugged terrain and the hidden riches it conceals. Togather we help this place thrive.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.guard.0=I am gladly following your invitation. For it is my sworn duty to protect the innocent, maintain order and ensure the peace among my people.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.guard.1=Bandits drove me from my home. Back then I was weak. That will never happen again, neither to me nor to the people I have swear to protect.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.guard.2=I am used to tough labor and don't shy away from the dangers of the night. If your people need protection, you are welcome to contact me.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.tanner.0=I am looking for a new place to do business. I hope you are in need of quality leather goods or share my interest in my craft.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.tanner.1=As my family was told, you are reaching out for help to bring both fashion and protection to this place. I accept the assignment.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.tanner.2=I spent my days working with the hides of various creatures. Perhaps I can enrich the lives of the people here with some of my skills.

mxbville:gui.letter_reply.weaver.0=If there's work to be done, I am on hand. I also know one thing or two about the handling of exquisite fabrics or custom-made garment. Whatever this place needs.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.weaver.1=The place I come from became too small for me. I simply couldn't find a place to unfold my textile craftsmanship. Maybe my luck lies here with you.
mxbville:gui.letter_reply.weaver.2=The thread of fate has led your invitation to my humble hands. Let me 
	
